WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.051
Type @ in a note. Today, Yesterday, Tomorrow and Now are still there. New at the end of the list: Date…

00:04.051 --> 00:07.420
Type "date" (or arrow down to the row) and press Enter.

00:07.420 --> 00:12.297
A calendar opens on today, already focused. Arrows move a day or a week, PageDown the month, Shift+PageUp a year back.

00:12.297 --> 00:15.533
Enter inserts the ISO date where the @ stood, and focus returns to the note.

00:15.533 --> 00:22.956
Or type the date outright: a digit jumps to the field, and the grid follows as you type.

00:22.956 --> 00:30.751
Escape leaves the text exactly as it was. With Vim mode on, h j k l move and t jumps back to today.
